# Security Hardening

Full reference: `starter-kit/20-security-hardening.md`. Firewall/proxy/WAF (Cloudflare recommended) is an infrastructure concern set up per deployment — this rule covers what's enforceable in code.

## Rules

- **Never reuse `PAYLOAD_SECRET`** for anything other than Payload's own auth token signing. A public/query-string secret (revalidate endpoint, webhook verification) is always a separate env var.
- **Secret comparison is constant-time** (`crypto.timingSafeEqual`), never a plain `!==` string compare, for any secret-gated endpoint.
- **Any endpoint gated by a secret in a query string or header gets rate limited** (`src/lib/rateLimit.ts` at minimum — real limit belongs at the WAF).
- **New auth-enabled collection**: confirm `maxLoginAttempts`/`lockTime` are set (Payload disables lockout by default if unset).
- **Public form collections**: `create: publicCreate`, never `read`/`update`/`delete` open to anonymous. Verify Turnstile (`src/lib/turnstile.ts`) and disposable email (`src/lib/disposableEmail.ts`) server-side before writing, plus Zod validation.
- **File upload collections**: `create`/`update`/`delete` explicitly `staffOnly` (or narrower) — never rely on Payload's implicit default. If SVG is an allowed mimeType, it may only ever be rendered via `next/image`/`<img>` — never `<object>`, `<embed>`, direct navigation, or `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.
- **Drafts are a security boundary, not just editorial** — any collection/global with `versions.drafts` must use `access.read: publicReadPublished`, never `publicRead`. See `19-draft-publish-workflow.md`.
- **New third-party service** (analytics, embed, API): update CSP `connect-src`/`img-src`/`script-src`/`font-src` in `next.config.mjs` — don't widen with a wildcard.
- **New security-relevant npm dependency**: verify it exists and is maintained (check the registry) before adding — don't trust a package name from memory.

## Review gate

- [ ] No secret reused across two different trust boundaries
- [ ] Constant-time compare on any secret check
- [ ] Rate limiting present on any publicly-reachable secret-gated or write endpoint
- [ ] File upload access explicit, not implicit
- [ ] CSP updated if a new external origin was introduced

